  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between GLPG-0492 and Prelamin-A/C through a series of molecular interactions. The drug GLPG-0492 is identified as a target of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-3, which is itself a target of a complex compound with a specific chemical structure. This compound further targets Prelamin-A/C, indicating a possible pathway where GLPG-0492 may influence the activity of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-3, which in turn affects Prelamin-A/C. Additionally, GLPG-0492 is also linked to Cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator, which is targeted by another compound that also affects Prelamin-A/C. These findings suggest that GLPG-0492 may exert its effects through a mechanism involving the modulation of enzymes or proteins that are involved in the regulation of Prelamin-A/C. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between GLPG-0492 and Prelamin-A/C, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
